peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.44) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The transcript's model download no longer fails on a packaged install.
    transcribe.py wrote models beside itself, which is /usr/share and read-only,
    so every transcript ended in "PermissionError ... /asr/models". It now uses
    its own folder when writable and ~/.local/share/peacemachine-dvd-ripper/asr
    otherwise.
  * A failed transcript now puts the real reason in the queue row instead of a
    flat "transcript pass failed".

